emily: Quick heads-up — opened a small PR that updates SDK snippets for cursor-based pagination + streaming resume behavior + retry guidance across Python/TS/Go. Link: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/842
alyssa: Nice. Is this mostly copy tweaks or code changes?
mike: Mostly code. I trimmed the JS example to show `async iterator` + explicit `retryWithJitter` helper. Small snippet:
```js
async function* streamPages() {
  let cursor = null;
  while (true) {
    const resp = await retryWithJitter(() => client.listItems({cursor}));
    for (const item of resp.items) yield item;
    if (!resp.next_cursor) break;
    cursor = resp.next_cursor;
  }
}
```
jordy: Go snippet needs `context` handling; current PR uses a plain timeout which can leak. I suggested:
```go
ctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(ctx, 10*time.Second)
defer cancel()
resp, err := client.ListItems(ctx, &ListReq{Cursor: cursor})
```
sanjay: Also: do we want to call out that streaming responses may omit a final cursor when the stream terminates early? I added a note in the docs.
emily: Yes, add explicit "best practice" note: save last-seen cursor only after successful page decode. Also add a short test case suggestion.
alyssa: For Python, small pattern to show `backoff` usage + iterator pattern:
```py
def page_iter(client):
    cursor = None
    while True:
        resp = backoff.on_exception(...)(lambda: client.list_items(cursor))()
        for i in resp['items']:
            yield i
        if not resp.get('next_cursor'):
            break
        cursor = resp['next_cursor']
```
mike: Pinged eng-runtime about semantics for "resume token TTL". They confirmed tokens expire after 5 minutes by default; added a TODO to show `expire_after` knob.
docs-bot: Preview deployed: https://deploy-preview-842--docs.redwood.ai
